+# Handoff
+
+## State
+Release is out, so `--wrap WIDTH` was re-applied from the patch below to `tabulate/cli.py` (uncommitted).
+Verified: csv input wraps at 12 with the ticket ID intact, `-w 0` exits 2 with usage, suite 375 passed / 8 skipped.
+Still TODO: tests (CLI has no test file), README mention, commit.
+
+## Design to resume after the release
+- `-w WIDTH` / `--wrap WIDTH` in `tabulate/cli.py`, passed to `tabulate()` as `maxcolwidths=WIDTH` (int, all columns).
+- Must also pass `break_long_words=False, break_on_hyphens=False`. Without them, ticket IDs and URLs are split
+  mid-token (`SUPPORT-2024-118233` -> `S`/`UPPORT-...`), which breaks copy-paste for support.
+  Trade-off: a word longer than WIDTH overflows the column rather than being cut.
+- Width must be a positive integer; otherwise print error + usage, exit 2 (same as other getopt errors).
+- Headers are not wrapped. No tests or README changes were written yet; the CLI has no test file.
+- Verified manually and the existing suite passed (358 passed) with the change applied.
+
+## Full patch (apply with `git apply`)
+```diff
+diff --git a/tabulate/cli.py b/tabulate/cli.py
+index cfae6fe..2ef62b7 100644
+--- a/tabulate/cli.py
++++ b/tabulate/cli.py
